  "body_html": "<h1>Lottery</h1>\n<p>For a finite set of outcomes $O$, a lottery is a probability distribution on\n$O$. The degenerate lottery at $o\\in O$ assigns probability one to $o$.</p>\n<p>Given lotteries $L_1,L_2$ and a scalar $\\alpha\\in[0,1]$, the compound lottery\n$$\n  [\\alpha L_1,(1-\\alpha)L_2]\n$$\nis the lottery assigning each outcome the probability\n$$\n  \\alpha L_1(o)+(1-\\alpha)L_2(o).\n$$</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MSZ, Chapter 2, Definitions 2.9-2.11] Maschler, Solan, and Zamir, <em>Game Theory</em>, <code>references/GameTheory.pdf</code>. Lotteries, degenerate lotteries, and compound lotteries.</li>\n</ul>",
